      summary: "On September 4, 2026, Jovia Financial Federal Credit Union filed a $17.1 million foreclosure suit in Cook County Circuit Court against S Indiana Avenue LLC, an entity controlled by Lakewood, New Jersey investor Reuven Y. Rivlin, over a 10-story, 129,200-square-foot office building at 1911-1921 South Indiana Avenue. The credit union says the borrower defaulted on a $17.5 million mortgage after a three-month forbearance agreement expired in June. The building's primary tenant, a state agency that leased space for the Department of Children and Family Services, stopped paying rent after December 2025, and a state spokesperson told The Real Deal the lease was terminated for cause.",
