      summary: "German bank Helaba (Landesbank Hessen-Thüringen Girozentrale), which made a $50 million mortgage on 29 West 34th Street in 2018, sued Jeff Sutton's 29 West 34 Owner LLC to foreclose in September 2025 after sending default notices over unpaid real estate taxes. In July 2026 Helaba assigned the mortgage to 29 W. 34th Street Holdings LLC, which passed it to 29 W. 34th Street Lender LLC; The Real Deal reported that SL Green's chief legal officer, Andrew S. Levine, is an executive vice president of the Holdings entity. On August 5, 2026, the owner, the new lender and the receiver signed a stipulation to discharge receiver Ian Lagowitz, return control to the owner and dismiss the case without prejudice, pending Judge Francis Kahn III's signature.",
