      summary: "Blue Sky Towers IV LLC sued the Town of Waldoboro, Maine, its Board of Appeals and its Planning Board in the U.S. District Court for the District of Maine on September 11, 2026, Wireless Estimator reported. The suit follows the Board of Appeals' unanimous August 20 denial of a variance for a 194-foot tower at 2734 Friendship Road, about five miles from Route 1, where a town rule confines wireless facilities to within 300 yards of that road. Blue Sky alleges the denial effectively prohibits personal wireless service in violation of the Telecommunications Act and lacked substantial evidence.",
