      summary: "Seven Baltimore residents sued the Mayor and City Council of Baltimore, the City Council, the Board of Estimates and MCB HP Baltimore LLC in the Circuit Court for Baltimore City on September 21, 2026, seeking to block MCB Real Estate's $900 million plan to demolish and replace the Harborplace pavilions, Baltimore Fishbowl reported. The 31-page complaint asks the court to declare void three 2023 City Council bills that changed zoning and removed height limits for the project, along with the city's March 31, 2023 lease with MCB. It alleges the bills are unconstitutional \"special laws\" and that the city granted MCB rights in public parkland without following the City Charter's franchise procedures. The city said it would reserve comment for court, and MCB had not responded to a request for comment.",
