        "American Hospitality Properties REIT, Inc. and 15 affiliates, including American Hospitality Properties REIT II, Inc., filed voluntary Chapter 11 petitions on October 4, 2026 in the U.S. Bankruptcy Court for the Northern District of Texas, WhatNow reported, citing PACER records. The affiliates include a master-lease entity and hotel-owning entities in locations including Cape Canaveral, Bentonville, Baton Rouge, Fayetteville, Fort Myers, Jonesboro, Metairie and Charlotte. The REITs own hotels operated under Marriott and Hilton brands; WhatNow noted the petition does not indicate that either hotel company owns the REIT. The case, No. 26-80071, is assigned to Judge Stacey G.C. Jernigan.",
