      summary: "White Sulphur Springs Holdings LLC, a company set up by TRT Holdings, the parent of Omni Hotels, sued Greenbrier Hotel Corporation, related Greenbrier entities and members of the Justice family in the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of West Virginia on April 9, 2026, seeking a receiver for The Greenbrier resort after acquiring the resort's loan debt previously held by Carter Bank & Trust. The Justice family countersued in Greenbrier County Circuit Court, alleging TRT and Carter Bank conspired to take the resort, which TRT called false. On August 14, 2026, after the family closed a joint venture with Kennedy Lewis Investment Management, the parties stipulated to dismiss the federal case with prejudice, and the state case was also dismissed, The Intermountain reported.",
