      summary: "The scheduled auction of Rochester's Hungerford Building is on hold after the attorney for the building's owner and affiliated LLCs appealed the foreclosure judgment, the Rochester Business Journal reported on October 15, 2026. The appeal argues Monroe County Supreme Court Justice Daniel J. Doyle erred in granting summary judgment because he relied on a flawed referee's report, which found $10,490,036.37 owed to mortgage holder Elizon DB Transfer Agent. Doyle approved the report and granted the foreclosure judgment on September 2, 2026, after rejecting the defendants' earlier challenge to the calculations.",
